@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM608xoq -->
Verified: the finding is real but pre-existing and additive. The gap (a private path added in one retained commit and removed by a later one, so both endpoint scans miss it) is not introduced by this PR; GH#37163 scopes this PR to scanning the public diff before validators. The reviewer also labels it a follow-up.

Per review-bot-gate policy, not expanding this PR. Follow-up recommended: scan each retained (non-WIP) commit's added lines in `privacy_scan_public_diff` (`.agents/scripts/privacy-guard-helper.sh`) and the pre-push hook (`.agents/hooks/privacy-guard-pre-push.sh`), keeping WIP-commit handling. Verify with a two-commit add-then-remove private path scenario.

@coderabbitai Verified and addressed in the pushed branch (98732a2fa, integrated at 1f7c708d1). `.agents/scripts/pulse-dispatch-worker-systemd.sh:279-280` now tests variable presence using `${VAR+x}`, so an empty assignment reports `set=yes` without exposing values.

Verification: ShellCheck and `bash -n` passed; `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-worker-spawn-fail-fast.sh` passed all 10 cases; direct checks under `bash -u` passed all 9 unset/empty/non-empty combinations. The concurrently pushed equivalent fix was preserved through a clean merge.

<!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM609aYP -->

@coderabbitai Addressed in 52d26c845. `.agents/scripts/setup/modules/mcp-setup.sh:462,480,490` now prints command-bearing messages with `%s`, interpreting only the color arguments with `%b`. This preserves `%q` backslashes without changing shared print helpers.

Verified: `bash -n .agents/scripts/setup/modules/mcp-setup.sh`, `git diff --check`, and focused execution of installed, declined-install, and failed-install paths using a helper path containing spaces and a literal backslash; all displayed commands round-trip to the original helper path. Commit/push hooks passed; direct ShellCheck was unavailable because the wrapper lacks its underlying binary. Push hook deferred TypeScript checking to CI because `tsc` is absent.

<!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM60-l3c -->

@coderabbitai Addressed in 52d26c845. `.agents/scripts/setup/modules/mcp-setup.sh:462` now displays separate explicit `status` and `pair` invocations. The helper dispatch at `.agents/scripts/opencode-browse-helper.sh:335-342` confirms that these select the intended operations rather than default help.

Verified Bash syntax, whitespace checks, and focused execution of the installed path: both displayed commands parse to the exact helper path plus the corresponding subcommand, including spaces/backslashes in that path. Commit/push hooks passed; direct ShellCheck was unavailable (missing underlying binary), and the push hook deferred TypeScript checking to CI because `tsc` is absent.

